{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_jev_playground", "label": "Jev Playground (weekly benchmark repo)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1-L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A weekly series that builds something real with Jev and publishes the measurements, on the premise that the useful question is not 'is Jev better than Claude' but which steps of a workflow are decisions and which are writing."}, {"id": "readme_typesafe_ai", "label": "TypeSafe AI (Jev vendor)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L3", "source_url": "https://www.typesafe.ai/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "label": "Jev typed decision model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L6-L10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "You send state plus typed questions and get back a choice, a score, or a probability with a confidence. It cannot write prose, and that is the point: output is a label and a number, so input bills at $42 per billion tokens and output is free."}, {"id": "readme_house_rules", "label": "House rules for the benchmarks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L25-L56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Six self-imposed rules written as a reaction to vendor benchmarks; they are the reason the numbers here are lower than the ones in launch posts."}, {"id": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "label": "House rule: the answer key is written by hand", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L31-L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If a model writes the labels, scoring that model against them measures self-agreement and quietly penalises every other model for disagreeing. Every label is hand-written against a published rubric you can argue with."}, {"id": "readme_shared_prompt_spec", "label": "House rule: both sides get the same words", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L36-L38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prompts are generated from one shared spec file. Jev gets the criteria as typed questions, Claude gets the same strings rendered as text, so neither sees wording the other did not get and accuracy differences are attributable to the model."}, {"id": "readme_fix_the_unfair_thing", "label": "House rule: fix the unfair thing even when it helps the other side", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L40-L44", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first version of the table was wrong in Claude's disfavour (thinking on by default, cache reads billed at list price). A benchmark that only corrects in one direction is not worth publishing."}, {"id": "readme_measure_the_network", "label": "House rule: measure the network, not just the model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L46-L49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev's first call looked like 970ms, but ~600ms was the TLS handshake and ~290ms was round trip time, leaving roughly 80ms of actual inference. Every latency number states which is which rather than folding the network floor into the model's number."}, {"id": "readme_publish_the_failures", "label": "House rule: publish the failures", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L51-L52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every raw response is committed to results/raw/, including the wrong ones, so a reader who distrusts a number can check it."}, {"id": "readme_say_where_the_other_thing_wins", "label": "House rule: say where the other thing wins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L54-L55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev cannot write an email; rather than asserting that, the repo asks the live API for a text question type and shows the HTTP 400."}, {"id": "readme_sample_size_caveat", "label": "Sample-size caveat (60 leads, one laptop, one afternoon)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L72-L80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "60 cases carries roughly plus or minus 8 points at 90% confidence and latency depends on location relative to the API, so the reader should take the shape of the result rather than the third decimal place. Cost is the number to trust, being token counts against published rates."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L6-L10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_typed_decision_model", "target": "readme_typesafe_ai", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_jev_playground", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L23", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules", "target": "readme_hand_written_answer_key", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L31", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_rules",